5: 
6: # Tasks: RBAC User Management
7: 
8: **Input**: Design documents from `/specs/001-rbac-user-management/`
9: 
10: **Prerequisites**: plan.md (required), spec.md (required for user stories), research.md,
11: data-model.md, contracts/
12: 
13: **Tests**: INCLUDED. The constitution (v2.0.0, Principle IV) mandates dual-sided
14: authorization tests (200 OK for permitted / 403 Forbidden for unauthorized) plus lockout
15: guardrail coverage, so every user story ships with its test suite.
16: 
17: **Organization**: Tasks are grouped by user story to enable independent implementation and
18: testing of each story.
19: 
20: ## Format: `[ID] [P?] [Story] Description`
21: 
22: - **[P]**: Can run in parallel (different files, no dependencies)
23: - **[Story]**: Which user story this task belongs to (e.g., US1, US2, US3)
24: - Include exact file paths in descriptions
25: 
26: ## Path Conventions
27: 
28: - Single Spring Boot Maven project at repository root.
29: - Java sources: `src/main/java/com/example/rbac/...`; tests:
30:   `src/test/java/com/example/rbac/...`; views: `src/main/resources/templates/...`.
31: - Contract details: `contracts/permissions.md`, `contracts/roles.md`, `contracts/users.md`.
32: 
