50: ## Phase 2: Foundational (Blocking Prerequisites)
51: 
52: **Purpose**: Core infrastructure that MUST be complete before ANY user story can be
53: implemented
54: 
55: **⚠️ CRITICAL**: No user story work can begin until this phase is complete
56: 
57: - [X] T004 [P] Create entities exactly per `data-model.md`: `User`, `Role`, `Permission`,
58:       `RolePermission`, `UserRole`, `AuditEvent` in `src/main/java/com/example/rbac/domain/`
59:       (UUID PKs, UTC timestamps, composite keys `(role_id, permission_id)` /
60:       `(user_id, role_id)`, cascade rules, optimistic `version` on Role/User)
61: - [X] T005 [P] Create Spring Data repositories for all six entities in
62:       `src/main/java/com/example/rbac/domain/` (interfaces, incl. uniqueness queries)
63: - [X] T006 [P] Create centralized permission catalog constants class
64:       `src/main/java/com/example/rbac/security/Permissions.java` with every code from
65:       `contracts/README.md` (no magic strings — constitution Security Implementation
66:       Standards)
67: - [X] T007 Create `PermissionResolver` resolving effective permissions
68:       (User-Roles -> Roles -> Permissions, active only, active-user only) in
69:       `src/main/java/com/example/rbac/security/PermissionResolver.java` per D-1/research.md
70: - [X] T008 Create Spring Security configuration
71:       `src/main/java/com/example/rbac/security/SecurityConfig.java`: deny-by-default
72:       (`authorizeHttpRequests` whitelisting only `/login`, `/css/**`, `/js/**`,
73:       `/assets/**`, `/error`), form-login, `AuthorizationManager` delegating to
74:       PermissionResolver BEFORE controller dispatch, and exposing resolved permissions to
75:       Thymeleaf request attributes (contracts/README.md security conventions)
76: - [X] T009 Create `UserPrincipalService` in
77:       `src/main/java/com/example/rbac/security/UserPrincipalService.java` loading users by
78:       username (with ACTIVE check) and BCrypt password encoding, plus the `/login`
79:       Thymeleaf template in `src/main/resources/templates/login.html`
80: - [X] T010 [P] Create `AuditService` in `src/main/java/com/example/rbac/service/AuditService.java`
81:       appending `audit_event` rows (actor, action, target type/id, before/after, UTC
82:       timestamp) per FR-014/data-model.md
83: - [X] T011 [P] Create `GlobalExceptionHandler` in
84:       `src/main/java/com/example/rbac/web/GlobalExceptionHandler.java` mapping 403 (not
85:       authorized), 400 (validation), 404, and 409 (conflict) to error templates in
86:       `src/main/resources/templates/error/`
87: - [X] T012 [P] Create the CoreUI-backed base layout and permission-driven sidebar fragment
88:       in `src/main/resources/templates/fragments/` rendering menu/action links only for
89:       granted permissions (D-2, server-side source of truth)
90: - [X] T013 Create idempotent `DataSeeder` in `src/main/java/com/example/rbac/config/DataSeeder.java`:
91:       all permission catalog rows, protected "Super Admin" role (`isProtected=true`) with all
92:       permissions, and one seeded administrator user (`app.seed.admin-password`)
93: 
94: **Checkpoint**: Foundation ready — security pipeline, schema, seed data all present.
95: User story implementation can now begin.
