99: ## Phase 3: User Story 1 - Manage the Permission Catalog (Priority: P1) 🎯 MVP
100: 
101: **Goal**: Admins can list, create, view, deactivate, and reactivate permissions under a
102: fail-closed, permission-enforced flow.
103: 
104: **Independent Test**: Sign in as a user granted `permission.*` codes — full CRUD works;
105: sign in as a user with every code except them — 403 on all permission screens.
106: 
107: ### Tests for User Story 1 (write FIRST, ensure they FAIL before implementation)
108: 
109: - [X] T014 [P] [US1] Dual-sided authorization tests in
110:       `src/test/java/com/allensandiego/adm/security/PermissionAuthorizationTest.java` covering
111:       every GET/POST in `contracts/permissions.md`: granted role → 200, denied role → 403
112: - [X] T015 [P] [US1] Service tests in `src/test/java/com/allensandiego/adm/service/PermissionServiceTest.java`:
113:       unique code enforcement, blank/invalid code rejection, deactivate prevents new grants,
114:       reactivate restores availability (FR-002/FR-003/FR-012)
115: 
116: ### Implementation for User Story 1
117: 
118: - [X] T016 [US1] Implement `PermissionService` in
119:       `src/main/java/com/allensandiego/adm/service/PermissionService.java` (CRUD, activate/
120:       deactivate, uniqueness, active-only grants) — depends on T004–T006, T010
121: - [X] T017 [P] [US1] Implement `PermissionController` in
122:       `src/main/java/com/allensandiego/adm/web/PermissionController.java` (list w/ paging+search,
123:       new, detail, edit) per `contracts/permissions.md`
124: - [X] T018 [P] [US1] Create Permission Thymeleaf templates (list, new, detail, edit) in
125:       `src/main/resources/templates/permission/`
126: - [X] T019 [US1] Wire audit logging for permission mutations through `AuditService`
127:       (create, edit, deactivate, reactivate) with before/after values
128: - [X] T020 [US1] Verify full permission story: run
129:       `src/test/java/com/allensandiego/adm/security/PermissionAuthorizationTest.java` and
130:       `PermissionServiceTest.java` green; manual pass of Quickstart steps 1 and 6
131: 
132: **Checkpoint**: Permission catalog fully functional and independently testable — MVP.
