240: 
241: ## Dependencies & Execution Order
242: 
243: ### Phase Dependencies
244: 
245: - **Setup (Phase 1)**: No dependencies - can start immediately
246: - **Foundational (Phase 2)**: Depends on Setup completion - BLOCKS all user stories
247: - **User Stories (Phase 3+)**: All depend on Foundational completion
248:   - US1 (P1) → US2 (P2) → US3 (P3) recommended sequential (US2/3 integrate with the US1
249:     catalog & permission codes), but all technically parallel after Phase 2
250: - **Polish (Final Phase)**: Depends on all desired user stories being complete
251: 
252: ### User Story Dependencies
253: 
254: - **US1 (P1)**: Can start after Foundational - no dependencies on other stories
255: - **US2 (P2)**: Can start after Foundational - needs `permission.view` for the editor's
256:   active-permission list; still independently testable (seed data supplies catalog)
257: - **US3 (P3)**: Can start after Foundational - needs `role.view`/`permission.view` for the
258:   effective-permission panel; independently testable with seed data
259: 
260: ### Within Each User Story
261: 
262: - Tests written FIRST and FAILING before any implementation (constitution-mandated)
263: - Models/repos before services; services before controllers/views; audit wiring last
264: 
265: ### Parallel Opportunities
266: 
267: - Phase 1 setup tasks all marked [P] — independent files
268: - Phase 2 foundational tasks marked [P] — independent files
269: - Within each story the test tasks run in parallel, and controller/template tasks run in
270:   parallel after the service task
271: - Stories can be developed in parallel by different team members once Phase 2 completes
272: 
273: ---
274: 
275: ## Parallel Example: User Story 1
276: 
277: ```bash
278: # Launch all tests for User Story 1 together:
279: Task: "Dual-sided authorization tests in src/test/java/com/example/rbac/security/PermissionAuthorizationTest.java"
280: Task: "PermissionService tests in src/test/java/com/example/rbac/service/PermissionServiceTest.java"
281: 
282: # Launch implementation files (after service task) together:
283: Task: "PermissionController in src/main/java/com/example/rbac/web/PermissionController.java"
284: Task: "Permission Thymeleaf templates in src/main/resources/templates/permission/"
285: ```
286: 
287: ---
288: 
289: ## Implementation Strategy
290: 
291: ### MVP First (User Story 1 Only)
292: 
293: 1. Complete Phase 1: Setup
294: 2. Complete Phase 2: Foundational (CRITICAL - blocks all stories)
295: 3. Complete Phase 3: User Story 1
296: 4. **STOP and VALIDATE**: PermissionAuthorizationTest + PermissionServiceTest green; manual
297:    CRUD verified
298: 5. Deploy/demo if ready
299: 
300: ### Incremental Delivery
301: 
302: 1. Setup + Foundational → foundation ready (deny-by-default security live)
303: 2. US1 → permission catalog (MVP) → Test → Deploy/Demo
304: 3. US2 → roles + role-permission editor → Test → Deploy/Demo
305: 4. US3 → users + role assignment → Test → Deploy/Demo
306: 5. Each story adds value without breaking previous stories
307: 
308: ### Parallel Team Strategy
309: 
310: 1. Team completes Setup + Foundational together
311: 2. Once Foundational is done: Developer A = US1, Developer B = US2, Developer C = US3
312: 3. Stories integrate independently; US2/US3 consume the shared catalog/seeder
313: 
314: ---
315: 
316: ## Notes
317: 
318: - [P] tasks = different files, no dependencies
319: - [Story] label maps task to a specific user story for traceability
320: - Constitution governance: each new endpoint MUST carry 200/403 tests — enforced via the
321:   dual-sided suites in every story phase
322: - Commit after each task or logical group; stop at checkpoints to validate the story
323:   independently

